{"name":"Dark Void","hex":"#151517","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"void","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing nothing; empty; not occupied or filled.","Having no incumbent; unoccupied; said of offices etc."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An empty space; a vacuum.","An extended region of space containing no galaxies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/void"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark Void","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Void is a 2010 third-person shooter game developed by Airtight Games and published by Capcom. In the game, players must face an alien threat that humanity had previously banished. It was released for PlayStation 3, Windows, and Xbox 360 in January 2010. It received mixed reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ed/Dark_Void.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Void","wikidata":"Q604461"},{"title":"Void (astronomy)","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmic voids are vast spaces between filaments, which contain very few or no galaxies. In spite of their size, most galaxies are not located in voids but are gravitationally bound together, creating huge cosmic structures known as galaxy filaments. The cosmological evolution of the void regions differs drastically from the evolution of the universe as a whole: there is a long stage when the curvature term dominates, which prevents the formation of galaxy clusters and massive galaxies. Hence, although even the emptiest regions of voids contain more than ~15% of the average matter density of the universe, the voids look almost empty to an observer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Structure_of_the_Universe.jpg/330px-Structure_of_the_Universe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Void_(astronomy)","wikidata":"Q845371"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness","wikidata":"Q204170"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Galaxy_superclusters_and_galaxy_voids.png/500px-Galaxy_superclusters_and_galaxy_voids.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Galaxy_superclusters_and_galaxy_voids.png/500px-Galaxy_superclusters_and_galaxy_voids.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of galaxy voids","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGalaxy_superclusters_and_galaxy_voids.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Large-scale_structure_formation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/Large-scale_structure_formation.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A 43×43×43-megaparsec cube shows the evolution of the large-scale structure over a logarithmic period starting from a redshift of 30 and ending at redshift 0. The matter-dense regions in the model contract under the collective gravitational force while simultaneously aiding in the expansion of cosmic voids as the matter flees to the walls and filaments.","link":"https://